    1 : // ============================================================
    2 : // step_strain_tape_transient.edp
    3 : // Strain-defect single-tape transient scenario: NO slit, NO heater. Current
    4 : // is ramped to just above the tape's NOMINAL (undamaged) critical current,
    5 : // and the ONLY quench trigger is a strain-induced Jc defect (from real
    6 : // ANSYS strain data via strain_to_jc.py's Ekin-Weibull pipeline). Full LN
    7 : // bath immersion -- Dirichlet 77K on EVERY boundary face, not just the two
    8 : // current-lead ends (unlike every other track in this repo).
    9 : //
   10 : // Electrical model: ONE equipotential channel along x (no slit to split
   11 : // it, and no slit-style voltage-matching bisection needed either -- there's
   12 : // only one continuous REBCO sheet here, not two physically severed
   13 : // conductors, so E(x) is genuinely a single shared value across z at each
   14 : // x). The per-x bisection is Z-RESOLVED: the REBCO current-sharing term is
   15 : // a proper integral over z of sigmaScDefect(E, T(x,z), jcRatioOfXZ(x,z)),
   16 : // not a single width-averaged scalar -- so current redistribution away
   17 : // from a narrow, severe width-edge defect (found in real strain data, see
   18 : // strain-defect/CLAUDE.md) is represented directly, at the SAME E(x) every
   19 : // z-strip shares. This replaced an earlier width-averaged hybrid design
   20 : // once real data showed a defect severe/narrow enough that averaging was
   21 : // unconservative. The volumetric Joule-heating source term is unaffected
   22 : // by this change -- it already used the full 2D jcRatioOfXZ(x,z) field
   23 : // pointwise (see sourceOfDefect below).
   24 : // ============================================================
   25 : 
   26 : real tInvocationStart = clock();
   27 : 
   28 : real tMeshStart = clock();
   29 : include "hts_mesh_module_tape.idp"// ============================================================
    2 : // hts_mesh_module_tape.idp
    3 : // 3D shell mesh for the strain-defect single-tape model: NO slit, 6mm wide,
    4 : // 115mm long (matches the real ANSYS strain export's LOCZ span, 0-115mm --
    5 : // resized from an initial 80mm placeholder once real data showed the actual
    6 : // specimen is longer; see strain-defect/CLAUDE.md). 5-layer cross-section
    7 : // (down from the 6-7 layers in 3D/3D-slit):
    8 : // a single merged Cu conductor wraps the full perimeter (bottom 1um + top
    9 : // 21um [1um electroplate + 20um stabilizer, merged into one region since
   10 : // they're electrically/thermally identical copper] + both side edges 1um),
   11 : // then Hastelloy/Buffer/REBCO/Ag-top as inner-stack-only layers, same
   12 : // "inner stack only" pattern as 3D/3D-slit's non-Cu layers. No bottom Ag
   13 : // (removed per design discussion) -- see strain-defect/CLAUDE.md.
   14 : //
   15 : // Region numbering (bottom to top):
   16 : //   1 = Cu (merged wrap: bottom + top + both side edges, ONE conductor)
   17 : //   2 = Hastelloy (20um, diminished from the 3D/3D-slit tracks' 50um)
   18 : //   3 = Buffer (0.2um)
   19 : //   4 = REBCO (1um)
   20 : //   5 = Ag top (2um)
   21 : //
   22 : // cube()'s native boundary labels (UNCHANGED convention from 3D/3D-slit,
   23 : // confirmed by area in mesh_report_strain_tape.edp, not assumed): 1/3 =
   24 : // y-lateral walls (bottom/top), 2/4 = x-end faces (current leads), 5/6 =
   25 : // z-lateral walls (side edges). Unlike every existing track, THIS model's
   26 : // step script applies the LN-bath Dirichlet condition to ALL SIX labels
   27 : // (full immersion), not just 2/4 -- see step_strain_tape_transient.edp.
