   54 : // rampRateTarget/rampDt: same slow-ramp machinery already validated in
   55 : // 3D-slit/electrothermal (see that track's CLAUDE.md) -- below-Ic ramp is
   56 : // thermally quasi-static regardless of duration, so a coarse rampDt there
   57 : // is safe. Default ratio here is >1 (this scenario's whole point is
   58 : // pushing past nominal Ic), so tCrossIc is meaningfully BEFORE Tramp.
   59 : real rampRateTarget = getARGV("-ramprate", 0.0);
   60 : real rampDt = getARGV("-rampdt", 0.05);
   61 : real rampDtAboveIc = getARGV("-rampdt-aboveic", 0.002);
   62 : real maxJcFracChange = getARGV("-maxjcfracchange", 0.05);
   63 : real Tramp = 0.5;
   64 : if (rampRateTarget > 0.0) Tramp = I0Target/rampRateTarget;
   65 : real tCrossIc = (currentRatio > 1.0) ? Tramp/currentRatio : Tramp;
   66 : // No heater pulse in this scenario -- tEnd is just Tramp plus a
   67 : // configurable post-ramp hold window to observe the defect-triggered
   68 : // quench (or its absence) develop.
   69 : real postRampHold = getARGV("-postramphold", 3.0);
   70 : real tEnd = Tramp + postRampHold;
